======================================================================================================================
L7 -- is the cluster residual the cosmic dark-to-baryon share?
======================================================================================================================
    cosmic Omega_dm/Omega_b = 5.43; clusters retain 70-100% of the cosmic baryon share at R500,
    so the LambdaCDM expectation for M_dark/M_bar is 5.4-7.8, and it should be nearly universal.

    alt: 12 clusters at r = 1000 kpc median (0.80 R500)
      baryon fraction f_bar        : median 0.149  [0.115, 0.160]
      NEWTONIAN  M_dark/M_bar      : median 5.73  +/- 0.68  (12% scatter)   [cosmic 5.43]
      FRAMEWORK  M_resid/M_bar     : median 2.76  +/- 0.72  (26% scatter)   [framework predicts 0]
      framework residual radial trend d(ratio_F)/dlog r: median -1.97 per dex
